  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "Given that the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is $17$, find all the possible values of $p$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & p & 4 \\\\ 6 & -2 & p\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **ascending order**, the values of $p$ are\n\n$p=$ \n{{field-1}} $\\,$ and $\\,p=$\n{{field-2}}.",
  "worked_solution": "To evaluate the minor of ${a}_{11},$ we remove the first row and first column:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & \u2217 & \u2217 \\\\ \u2217 & p & 4 \\\\ \u2217 & -2 & p\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}p & 4 \\\\ -2 & p\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}p & 4 \\\\ -2 & p\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =p\\cdot p-4\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & ={p}^{2}+8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is $17$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{2}+8 & =17 \\\\ {p}^{2}-9 & =0 \\\\ (p-3)(p+3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $p=-3$ and $p=3.$",
